ences\nCollege of Liberal Arts\nCollege of Life & Physical Sciences\nCollege of Public Service\nAcademic Programs\nHonors College\nRegistrar\nLibraries & Media Center\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nCampus Tour\nFinancial Aid\nScholarships\nTuition & Costs\nFAQ\u2019s\nStudent Life\nActivities\nHousing\nBookstore\nThe Meter\nLeadership & Organizations\nService Learning\nOffice of Technology Services (OTS)\nWeb Services\nResearch\nInstitutional Research\nResearch Centers of Excellence\nAthletics\nMake a Gift\nMYTSU Login\nFAQ | Biology | College of Life & Physical Sciences\nBiology\nFaculty\nStudent Resources\nTeachers Certification\nProject Tiger Teach\nFAQ\nExplore Colleges & Schools\nBiology\nFaculty\nStudent Resources\nTeachers Certification\nProject Tiger Teach\nFAQ\nFrequently Asked Questions\n1. What are the course requirements for minor in biology?\n\u2013 An under graduate minor in biology consists of a minimum of 24 semester hours of biology courses, 16 of which should be taken in sequence. These courses are BIOL 1110/ 1111 General Biology I and Lab; BIOL 1120/ 1121 General Biology II and Lab; BIOL 2110/2111 Cell Biology and Lab, and BIOL 2120/ 2121 Principles of Genetics and Lab. General Chemistry 1110 and 1120, with laboratories, are required as a supporting related course and must precede BIOL 2110. The remaining eight hours of biology courses must be on the 3000 or 4000 level and may be elected by the student.\n2. How do I know who my faculty advisor is?\n\u2013 You can find the name and contact email of your biology faculty advisor from your Degree Works, which is located within your MyTSU Portal. Logon to your MyTSU, click on Degree Works, then you will see the name of your faculty advisor.\n3. What are the upper division general elective courses for undergraduate biology major?\n\u2013 Upper division general elective courses can be in any discipline, having a course number greater than 3000.\n4. How can I officially change my major, minor or concentration?\n\u2013 You may officially change your major, add or drop a minor or double major, change your concentration by submitting a request form. You may download the blank Undergraduate Change of Major/Minor Request Form, fill in required information, ask your advisor to sign, and submit the form to the Office of Records.\nSearch for Courses\nAcademic Calendar\nUndergraduate Catalog\nGraduate Catalog\nDr. Elaine D. Martin\nProfessor and Interim Department Chair\nDepartment of Biological SciencesEmail: EMARTIN@Tnstate.edu(615) 963-5769On the Main Campus, the Department of Biological Sciences is housed in Harned Hall and McCord Hall.\nBiological Sciences\n(615) 963-5769Chemistry\n(615) 963-5321Mathematical Sciences\n(615) 963-5869College of Life and Physical Sciences\n(615) 963-5811\nEvents & Announcements\nStay up to date with what's going on around campus\nJoin Our Newsletter\nSubscribe to receive the latest Tennessee State University news, events, and important updates.\nCompany\nThis field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged.\nEmail\nSubmit\nBy subscribing you agree to with our Privacy Policy\nAlumni\nAlumni\nTSU Foundation\nSupport\nHomecoming\nEstate Planning\nAdmissions\nAdmissions\nTuition & Costs\nFinancial Aid\nTransfer\nCampus Tour\nAbout\nAbout\nCampus\nPresident\nBoard of Trustees\nNondiscrimination Statement\nUniversity Calendar\nResearch\nSMART AI Center\nCampus Map\nTitle III\nContact\n3500 John A Merritt Blvd\nNashville, TN 37209\nTel: (615) 963-5000\nHelp Desk Ticket\nHelp Desk Phone: 615-963-7777\n\u00a9 Tennessee State University. All Rights Reserved.\n|\nJLB - Nashville Web Design & SEO + AI Search", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.tnstate.edu/academics/life-physical-sciences/departments/biology/faq/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.tnstate.edu"], ["Academics", "https://www.tnstate.edu/academics/"], ["Colleges", "https://www.tnstate.edu/academics"], ["College of Agriculture", "https